  "Question": "Car rental Plan A costs 100 yuan per day plus 2 yuan/km; Plan B costs 50 yuan per day plus 3 yuan/km. How many km must be driven in a day for the two plans to cost the same? (Unit: km)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "50",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let the distance driven be \\(x\\) km. Then \\(100+2x=50+3x\\). Solving gives \\(x=50\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Balance the daily fee with distance savings\n\nPlan A costs \\(100-50=50\\) yuan more in daily fees but saves \\(3-2=1\\) yuan per kilometre. The costs become equal when the distance savings cover that extra daily fee. Thus the required distance is\n\\[\n\\frac{100-50}{3-2}=50\\text{ km}.\n\\]",
